          "text": "\n\n\n=== CURRENT ITERATION: 2 ===\n\n\n=== BOUND VARIABLES ===\n\n- `history`: `list[HistoryItem]`, read-only, 1 entry\n\nSchema:\ntype HistoryItem =\n  | { kind: \"message\", id: str, role: enum[\"user\", \"system\", \"assistant\", \"event\"], content: str, attachments?: list[HistoryAttachment] }\n  | { kind: \"lashlang_step\", id: str, protocol_iteration: int, code: str, output: list[str], images?: list[HistoryImage], error?: str | null, final_output?: any | null }\ntype HistoryAttachment = { id: str, media_type?: str | null, label?: str | null, source: str, reference: str }\ntype HistoryImage = { id: str, media_type: str, width?: int | null, height?: int | null, bytes: int, label?: str | null }\n\n\n=== FINALIZATION ===\n\nFinish-required: prose alone never ends this turn. Every response performs its next step in an `execute_code` call, and the last one calls `finish <value>` (`finish null` only when null is the answer). Never announce an action without the `execute_code` call that performs it. The value must match the REQUIRED OUTPUT contract.\n\n=== REQUIRED OUTPUT ===\n\nstr",
